title: Duplicates and sync
tags: Duplicates
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: Duplicate data is never synchronised: each repository scans its own content.

`mfr_duplicate_group`, `mfr_inode`, `mfr_hash_mtime` and `mfr_hash_size` are
`mfr_*` fields other than `mfr_path`, which sync's field diff never writes:
they are derived from each repository's own files, and each side re-derives its
own. "Has a duplicate" is a property of one repository's content. Group
metarecords have no `mfr_path`, so no placement, and nothing synced references
them.

One correction was needed for that to hold: sync's referential closure followed
''every'' `ref`-valued field, so it materialised an empty group metarecord on the
other side for each group, because member files point at it. The closure now
skips the fields the diff does not write (`mfr_*` other than `mfr_path`), in
`core/src/sync/plan.rs` (`ref_targets`). The gap predated duplicate detection —
no `mfr_*` field had been a `ref` before `mfr_duplicate_group`.
